	<description>	

		We are TEAM UGLY, an Independent developer team established in Barcelona, ​​focused on the research and crafting of rare videogames.



	</description>

		

	<histories>
		<history>

			<header>Team Ugly</header>

			<text>
				Imagine an old workshop lost in the narrow streets of an old town, if you know the boss  you will be able to access to the backroom and look into these unique video games dragees carefuly preserved for you.
			</text>

		</history>

		

		<history>

			<header>People</header>

			<text>Gerard, David, Rita and Jaime met each other in Poblenou, Barcelona, sharing a creative space for coworking. Until they realized that they were sharing something more than a space for working: a perverse passion for video games. </text>

		</history>
		<history>

			<header>Rita Fortuny</header>

			<text>CEO. Since 2017, Rita leads development projects with a strong sense of art. With a deep background in UI and UX, she left business consulting to marry just one project: UGLY.   </text>

		</history>

		<history>

			<header>Gerard Singuerlin</header>

			<text>Game designer and artist. 10 years of experience as an animator and illustrator that pushes this creative side of TEAM UGLY. </text>

		</history>


		<history>

			<header>David Rodriguez</header>

			<text>Programmer and in charge of narrative. One of the few beings who master black and white arts. More than 15 years as a computer engineer and 6 years at the head of creative projects for kids. But one day his heart darkened, he pushed the kids out of the way and brought UGLY to life.   </text>

		</history>

	
		<history>

			<header>Jaime Vicente</header>

		<text>Technical artist. He was infected by UGLY from the beginning. His long career as an artist and his eccentric gaits help us to consolidate art and programming.   </text>

		</history>
		
	</histories>

		

